  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Addressing protection and sexual and reproductive health needs of flash flood affected women, adolescents and transgenders, including pregnant women and women with disabilities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main goal of this project is to provide sexual and reproductive health (SRH) assistance and protection against Gender Based Violence (GBV) to vulnerable people, mostly women and girls, affected by floods in the Chattogram division. This UNFPA project provides cash support, hygiene and clinical care kits, and psychosocial support for women and girls. This project provides sexual and reproductive health assistance to a total of 13,250 people, of whom 7,700 are women, 5,300 are girls, 250 are men, and 180 people with disabilities. In addition, 8,600 women are protected against gender-based violence.</narrative>
  </description>
